Package: hyperspectR
Title: Hyperspectral Imaging Analysis for Biomedical Applications
Version: 0.2.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("R.", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@charite.de",
        role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742")),
    person("V.", "Forstmeier", role = "aut"))
Description: Read, process, analyze, and visualize hyperspectral imaging (HSI)
    data from Cubert snapshot cameras and standard ENVI/TIFF formats. Provides
    calibration workflows (dark correction, white reference normalization),
    spectral preprocessing (Savitzky-Golay smoothing, SNV, MSC, derivatives),
    dimensionless spectral indices, research hemoglobin fraction fitting,
    dimensionality reduction (PCA, MNF), pixel classification (SAM, SVM,
    random forest), and constrained spectral unmixing. Includes an interactive
    'shiny' explorer, reproducible batch recipes and grouped evaluation tools.
    Results are research outputs; clinical or device-specific accuracy is not
    established by the included synthetic examples.
